Production Node.js dependencies:
  Original license and notice files are retained in node_modules/.
  third-party/node/overrides.json records version-specific supplemental
  license texts, their upstream sources and SHA-256 values.
  third-party/node/licenses/ contains these unchanged upstream texts.
  Packaged distributions include THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt with the full texts
  and third-party/node/inventory.json with every installed production
  package, version, document path and SHA-256.
  Generate the distribution with npm run package. From the module directory,
  verify it offline with node scripts/licenses.mjs dist --check.
  From inside the distribution, run node scripts/licenses.mjs . --check.

FFmpeg and platform runtimes:
  Keep third-party/ffmpeg/ and scripts/build_ffmpeg.py with the distribution.
  third-party/ffmpeg/README.md identifies the corresponding FFmpeg source
  archive, build instructions and LGPL-2.1-or-later licensing.
  That directory also preserves musl, GCC runtime exception and MinGW-w64
  runtime notices. The binaries and their manifests are in resources/ffmpeg/.

Redistribution:
  Preserve LICENSE, NOTICE, THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt, third-party/ and the
  original dependency notices in node_modules/. Do not treat the
  application's MIT license as replacing a dependency's license.
